course: dictionary
lesson: 1672
title: Germs in dirty water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cholera is a serious illness caused by tiny germs called bacteria. You can catch it from dirty water or food. The writer gives you clues in the sentences around the word. «A cholera outbreak» means many people got ill at the same time, and the word «outbreak» is a clue for that.
explain: Look at this: «Cholera gives very bad diarrhoea and makes the body lose water quickly.» The words around it tell you cholera is dangerous, because the body loses water fast. «Without treatment cholera can kill», so treatment matters.
explain: Good news comes in the next clue. Clean water with salts and sugar, called rehydration, and medicine save most people. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Cholera is an illness caused by germs called bacteria.
fact: Cholera spreads through dirty water or food.
fact: «Cholera» gives very bad diarrhoea and makes the body lose water quickly.
fact: In 1854 the doctor John Snow mapped cholera cases in London and found many around one water pump.
fact: Clean water with salts and sugar, called rehydration, helps save most people with cholera.
exercise: «A cholera outbreak was found in the town.» What is cholera? | A sweet drink made with lemon | A kind of tall, old tower | *A serious illness caused by germs in dirty water or food | A game played in the street
exercise: Which two things help save most people with cholera? | Loud music and long naps | *Clean water with salts and sugar | Hot baths and cold milk
exercise: «In 1854 the doctor John Snow mapped cholera cases.» What does «mapped» most likely mean here? | Washed in a pump | *Drew a plan showing where the cases happened | Put on a list of pets | Cooked for dinner
test: «Sewers are big underground tunnels that carry dirty water and rain to treatment works.» What is a sewer? | A small garden shed | A mountain path | *A big underground tunnel that carries dirty water | A kind of sewing box
test: «London's main sewers helped end the city's outbreaks of cholera.» What helped end cholera outbreaks in London? | Tall bell towers | Bigger factories | More steam trains | *Big sewers that carried dirty water away
exam: «Crowded, dirty towns suffered from cholera.» Why did crowded, dirty towns suffer from cholera? | Because the towns had too few people | Because the towns had too many clean water pumps | *Because dirty water and poor cleaning let the germs spread | Because the towns had too many trees
